er dealer unleashes a cast of rampaging robotic crabs!","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522481/screencap/6960d8dc3b805.jpg"},{"title":"Public and Private","synopsis":"Tsukauchi's investigation into the Trigger network has hit a wall, and he turns to All Might for advice.","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522482/screencap/696a128740137.jpg"},{"title":"A Rational Man","synopsis":"Koichi's in double trouble, facing down a villain who might clobber him, and Eraser Head who might arrest him!","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522483/screencap/697356cd6814e.jpg"},{"title":"The Man Returns","synopsis":"Koichi and Pop get into more Trigger trouble, and we learn where Knuckleduster has been.","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522484/screencap/697c7c8553b97.jpg"},{"title":"Rain and Cloud","synopsis":"Koichi encounters Eraser Head, who reminiscences about his student days.","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522485/screencap/6985b7dd33e48.jpg"},{"title":"Glass Sky","synopsis":"When he was young, Aizawa's inexperience and awkward Quirk forced him to grapple with his self-esteem.","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522486/screencap/698f6a41c977e.jpg"},{"title":"A Sky with No Rain Left","synopsis":"When Aizawa was a younger, he and his friend Shirakumo were forced into a fight with a giant villain...","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522487/screencap/699841889b566.jpg"},{"title":"Farewell Party!","synopsis":"With his legal problems soon to be taken care of, Captain Celebrity makes plans to return to America.","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522488/screencap/69a1785549f34.jpg"},{"title":"Zero Hour","synopsis":"Captain Celebrity's farewell party begins, but the Scarred Man has some unpleasant surprises in store...","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522489/screencap/69aac09f163a9.jpg"},{"title":"Balloon Soul","synopsis":"Captain Celebrity tries to save the Sky Egg with Koichi's help, while reminiscing on what brought him here.","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522490/screencap/69b3d9b83e744.jpg"},{"title":"This Is a Hero!!","synopsis":"The Sky Egg falls as Captain Celebrity hits his limit, with only one person capable of saving the day...","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522491/screencap/69bd2dfcbed5d.jpg"},{"title":"Graduation and Career Path","synopsis":"Captain Celebrity returns to the United States, and Koichi must decide what to do with his future.","thumbnail":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/episode/11522492/screencap/69c656a5b2893.jpg"}],"fields":{},"episodes":{}}
